WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:05.800
Okay, so now you might ask, you know what?

00:06.040 --> 00:08.480
The CTAs are very similar to the views.

00:08.480 --> 00:12.920
We have a query and the output of this query is going to be like an object in the database.

00:12.920 --> 00:14.920
So what are the differences between them.

00:15.200 --> 00:16.160
Let's check this.

00:16.160 --> 00:20.480
Now let's say that in our database we have a table that has three columns A, B, c.

00:20.520 --> 00:24.360
And now what we can do we can go and create a view based on a query.

00:24.360 --> 00:28.200
So you create the DDL statement in order to create the view in the database.

00:28.200 --> 00:31.160
And of course the database is going to go and store the query in the database.

00:31.360 --> 00:32.840
And it's going to be empty.

00:32.840 --> 00:36.200
So there will be no data because views does not store any data.

00:36.200 --> 00:39.560
And the query of the view will not be yet executed.

00:39.560 --> 00:43.280
But now in the other hand, if you go and create a table using CTAs.

00:43.440 --> 00:46.960
So here again we have a query attached to the object to the table.

00:46.960 --> 00:48.280
So here what happens.

00:48.280 --> 00:53.000
The database has to execute the query in order to understand the structure.

00:53.240 --> 00:56.960
And as well the data that should be inserted inside the table.

00:56.960 --> 00:59.720
So our SQL query is going to be executed.

00:59.720 --> 01:03.520
And the result of the query is going to be inserted inside the table.

01:03.520 --> 01:08.320
So that means this new table is storing already the result of the query.

01:08.320 --> 01:11.360
So now this is the first differences between the table and view.

01:11.400 --> 01:17.690
As you create view the query will not be executed, and we don't have anything about the result of the

01:17.690 --> 01:18.130
query.

01:18.170 --> 01:24.410
Where in the cities we have already result of the query stored inside the table and everything is prepared.

01:24.410 --> 01:28.290
So now let's see what's going to happen once the user selects something from the view.

01:28.410 --> 01:35.130
So now the database is going to go for the first time executing the query of the view in order to fetch

01:35.130 --> 01:39.810
the data from the original table and then present it as a result for the user.

01:39.810 --> 01:45.090
But now in the other hand, if the user go and query the table that is created from the cities.

01:45.250 --> 01:46.370
So now what can happen?

01:46.410 --> 01:53.010
SQL will not execute again the query of the cities because the database already done that and prepared

01:53.010 --> 01:53.770
everything.

01:53.770 --> 01:57.250
So that means we are not querying anything from the original table.

01:57.250 --> 02:02.770
And the data can be directly fetched from the new table so the users can get immediately the results

02:02.770 --> 02:05.530
from our table that is created from the cities.

02:05.730 --> 02:08.970
So here comes the second difference between the tables and views.

02:09.130 --> 02:15.490
The views are slower than Chtis and that's because the database has here an extra task.

02:15.530 --> 02:19.410
It must execute the query of the view in order to get the data.

02:19.410 --> 02:24.650
But in the cities, the query is going to be faster than the view, because we have already executed

02:24.650 --> 02:26.780
everything and prepared it for the user.

02:26.780 --> 02:30.580
So that's why tables from CTAs are way faster than views.

02:30.580 --> 02:35.940
And now there is another difference and perspective about this, which is from my point of view, is

02:35.940 --> 02:37.580
more important than the performance.

02:37.580 --> 02:43.340
So now let's say that in the next day we are doing data updates on the original table, like we are

02:43.340 --> 02:46.340
doing updates on the column C and as well in the column B.

02:46.380 --> 02:49.860
So now let's see what this means for the user if they are using views.

02:49.860 --> 02:53.100
So the user in the next day is executing again the same query.

02:53.100 --> 02:58.260
And again here the database has to execute the query of the view in order to fetch the data from the

02:58.260 --> 02:59.300
original table.

02:59.300 --> 03:05.060
So that means today in the views we are getting different data than yesterday because we have a new

03:05.060 --> 03:11.380
data and new updates, and the user in the result can see as well the new updates and the fresh data.

03:11.380 --> 03:16.700
So the user is seeing exactly the status of the data in the original tables.

03:16.700 --> 03:21.740
But now let's see what's going to happen if the user go and query the table from the CTAs.

03:21.940 --> 03:26.660
So in the table of the CTAs, we are still having the data from yesterday.

03:26.700 --> 03:31.380
All those new updates from the original data will not be reflected in this new table.

03:31.420 --> 03:36.980
Because once the user selects something from this table, the database will not go and query or fetch

03:36.980 --> 03:42.140
the new changes from the original table, because we have already prepared the data from yesterday.

03:42.140 --> 03:49.740
So that means our user now is getting all data from the CTAs table, and the only way to get new, fresh

03:49.740 --> 03:54.580
data from the CTAs is to re-execute the CTS query.

03:54.580 --> 04:00.340
And of course, this is another step and it is harder to maintain the table from the CTS.

04:00.580 --> 04:05.620
And this is a big difference for the users between the views and the tables from the CTAs.

04:05.660 --> 04:06.900
Now think about views.

04:06.900 --> 04:12.380
You are ordering a pizza at restaurants, so every time you are querying the view, you are placing

04:12.420 --> 04:13.180
an order.

04:13.220 --> 04:18.020
The chef can go and make a pizza from scratch using the freshest ingredients.

04:18.020 --> 04:21.340
So that means you are always getting a fresh hot pizza.

04:21.380 --> 04:26.220
And think about that CTAs as like a frozen pizza from a grocery store.

04:26.340 --> 04:30.900
The pizza was prepared earlier and stored in the freezer, and if you want to eat it, you have to go

04:30.900 --> 04:32.300
and heat it up in the oven.

04:32.300 --> 04:37.260
But it's still not like a fresh pizza that is made on the spot and from the scratch.

04:37.260 --> 04:41.820
Now, I made myself hungry because I love pizza, so I think I'm gonna go for a quick break.
